    <article class="ba-body">
      <p>Moon milk is a warm, spiced milk drink made in the evening. Ashwagandha root has an earthy taste, so warming spices and a little honey round it out.</p>
      <h2 id="highlights">Highlights</h2><ul class="ba-hl"><li>Ready in 8 minutes.</li><li>Works with oat, almond or dairy milk.</li><li>Use a frother for a café-style finish.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="s0">You'll need</h2><p>1 cup milk · 1 tsp Veda Ashwagandha Powder · ¼ tsp cinnamon · pinch of cardamom and nutmeg · 1 tsp honey or maple syrup</p><h2 id="s1">Method</h2><p>Warm the milk gently — don't boil. Whisk in Ashwagandha and spices, turn off the heat, stir in honey and pour.</p>
      
      <div class="art-prod"><img src="{{ 'pouch-ashwagandha.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Ashwagandha Powder pouch" width="620" height="861" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div><span class="jr-meta">Featured in this article</span><h3>Ashwagandha Powder</h3><p>Traditionally used to support stress management, vitality, strength and overall wellness.*</p><div class="hero-ctas"><button class="btn sm" type="button" data-add="ashwagandha">Add — {{ all_products['ashwagandha-powder'].price | money }}</button><a class="btn ghost sm" href="/products/ashwagandha-powder">View product</a></div></div></div>
      <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2><details class="ba-faq"><summary>Which milk works best for golden moon milk?</summary><p>Oat, almond or dairy milk all work. Warm the milk gently without boiling, then whisk in the Ashwagandha and spices.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>Who should check with a professional before trying Ashwagandha?</summary><p>NCCIH advises that ashwagandha may be unsafe during pregnancy, and people with certain conditions or taking medications should speak to a healthcare provider first.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>Can I use a frother?</summary><p>Yes — a frother gives the drink a café-style finish.</p></details>
